\begin{thm}\label{thm: quantitative Mitchell}
 Let $G$ be a sub-Finsler Lie group. With respect to a tangent grading, consider the tangent metric $d_0$ on $G$ and the dilated metrics $d_\epsilon$. Then, there are a neighborhood $\Omega$ of $1$ in $G$ and $C>0$ such that 
 \begin{align}\label{thm: eq: quantitative mitchell0}
     -Cd_\epsilon(p,q)^{1/\beta}\epsilon^{\alpha_0/\beta}&\leq d_\epsilon(p,q)-d_0(p,q)
