theorem.content:
[\cite{BealsRocklandConjNecessary,HelfferRockland}]\label{intro_thm_main}
 Let $G$ be a simply connected graded nilpotent Lie group, $D$ a left-invariant differential operator on $G$ which is homogeneous of degree $k\in \mathbb{N}$ with respect to the grading on $G$. The following are equivalent \begin{enumerate}
 \item The differential operator $D$ is hypoelliptic 
  \item For any irreducibly non-trivial unitary representation of $G$, $\pi(D)$  is injective on smooth vectors.
  \item For any differential operator $D'$ (not necessarily left-invariant) homogeneous of degree $\leq k$, and $K\subseteq G$ compact subset, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that 
      \begin{equation}\label{eqn:maxi_hypo_intro}\begin{aligned}
        \norm{D'(f)}_{L^2(G)}\leq C(\norm{f}_{L^2(G)}+\norm{D(f)}_{L^2(G)}),\quad \forall f\in C^\infty_c(G)\text{ such that } \supp(f)\subseteq K.       
      \end{aligned}\end{equation}
 \end{enumerate}

